      "title": "Canva layoffs: design giant to cut or relocate more than 1,200 jobs in major restructure",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/04/canva-layoffs-job-cuts-restructure",
      "description": "<p>Chief executive Melanie Perkins describes job cuts as ‘without doubt the hardest moment in our thirteen-year history’ in email to staff</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Canva is cutting or relocating more than 1,200 jobs, representing 22% of its global workforce, as part of a major restructure that includes laying off staff who helped build the Australian-founded design platform.</p><p>The changes mirror a trend across the technology sector, where software companies are fighting to stay competitive against cheaper artificial intelligence disrupters while aggressively embedding AI tools themselves.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/04/canva-layoffs-job-cuts-restructure\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-04T00:14:49"
    },
    {
      "title": "Choice Shonky awards 2026: From ticket sellers and Virgin flight credits to a 25-hour laundry cycle",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/04/choice-2026-shonky-awards-virgin-ticketmaster-hisense-sony",
      "description": "<p>Australia’s worst products and services for the year have been named by  consumer advocacy group Choice</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Concert tickets that surge to $1,650, an airline pocketing $75m of unused flight credits and a washer/dryer cycle that takes 25 hours have all made the dishonour roll in consumer advocacy group Choice’s annual Shonky awards.</p><p>Now in their 21st year, the Shonkys spotlight Australia’s worst products and services as decided by Choice.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/04/choice-2026-shonky-awards-virgin-ticketmaster-hisense-sony\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-03T22:48:24"
    },
    {
      "title": "US midterm elections 2026 live updates: Annie Andrews stuns Republicans in South Carolina Senate race amid Democratic surge",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2026/nov/03/midterm-election-results-live-updates",
      "description": "<p>Annie Andrews adds to Democrats’ strong evening by defeating Darline Graham, who was tapped to replace her late brother Lindsey Graham</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2026/nov/03/midterm-elections-full-results-senate-house-governor-races\">Track live results from all 50 states</a></p></li><li><p>Senate full report: <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/03/democrats-senate-midterm-elections-results\">Democrats aim to retake chamber</a></p></li><li><p>House full report: <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/03/democrats-house-midterm-elections-results\">Democrats poised to flip chamber</a></p></li></ul><p>As we bring you the latest from around the country, Donald Trump is certainly paying attention. From the White House, the president said that he was tuning into coverage on Fox News.</p><p><strong>“I can’t stand Jessica Tarlov’s voice,”</strong> Trump said of the Democratic strategist and Fox News contributor in<a href=\"https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/117554852721008421\"> a post on Truth Social</a>. The president called Tarlov <strong>“DUMB AS A ROCK”</strong>.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2026/nov/03/midterm-election-results-live-updates\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-04T03:38:59"
    },
    {
      "title": "Democrats poised to flip House in midterm elections after two turbulent years of Trump",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/03/democrats-house-midterm-elections-results",
      "description": "<p>Victory for party comes despite unusual and aggressive efforts by Republicans to redraw congressional districts</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2026/nov/03/midterm-election-results-live-updates\">US midterm elections – live updates</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2026/nov/03/midterm-elections-full-results-senate-house-governor-races\">Track live results from all 50 states</a></p></li></ul><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats\">Democrats</a> are winning competitive House races and are expected to flip the <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/house-of-representatives\">US House of Representatives</a> after two tumultuous years of Donald Trump’s second presidency. A change in House control would give Democrats a perch to conduct robust oversight of the administration for its final two years.</p><p>Republicans <a href=\"https://pressgallery.house.gov/member-data/party-breakdown\">currently</a> hold 218 seats in the House and Democrats have 214. (There is one vacancy in a Republican seat and one vacancy in a Democratic seat, and one Republican member switched his party affiliation to independent.) Democrats need to flip just three seats to gain control of the House.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/03/democrats-house-midterm-elections-results\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-04T03:24:28"
    },
    {
      "title": "Democrat Annie Andrews flips South Carolina Senate seat held by Republicans since 1998",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/03/south-carolina-midterms-annie-andrews",
      "description": "<p>Andrews ran a campaign on healthcare affordability and beat Darline Graham, sister of Lindsey Graham to win</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2026/nov/03/midterm-election-results-live-updates\">US midterm elections – live updates</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2026/nov/03/midterm-elections-full-results-senate-house-governor-races\">Track live results from all 50 states</a></p></li></ul><p>Democrat <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/jul/26/south-carolina-democrat-lindsey-graham-senate-seat\">Annie Andrews</a>, a <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/aug/31/annie-andrews-south-carolina-senate\">pediatrician</a> who campaigned on healthcare affordability, has won the race for <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-senate\">US Senate</a> in <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/south-carolina\">South Carolina</a>, making her the first Democrat to represent the state in the Senate for over a quarter century.</p><p>Andrews had faced an uphill battle in what has been seen as a reliably Republican state against Darline Graham, the sister of the late Republican powerbroker Lindsey Graham.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/03/south-carolina-midterms-annie-andrews\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-04T03:16:57"
